897:{"timestamp":"2026-07-23T07:54:15.040Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_05e80824f59ba654016a61c8a1ccec8194a02d35562473f7b4","status":"completed","call_id":"call_blqs1BaAG0JVbmD2yG2fw9Kd","name":"apply_patch","input":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /work/verification.k\n@@\n-  // An inert observation point used by the setup claim.  It marks the exact\n-  // generated While statement without executing or summarizing its body.\n-  syntax KItem ::= #primeLoopEntry(Int) | \"#capturePrimeLoopEntry\"\n+  // Proof-only observation points used by the setup claim.  They stop at the\n+  // generated While statement and capture its live n and divisor values;\n+  // they do not summarize or execute the loop body.\n+  syntax KItem ::= #primeLoopEntry(Int, Int)\n+                 | \"#capturePrimeLoopN\"\n+                 | #capturePrimeLoopD(Int)\n   rule <k>\n          While(_C:Expr, _B:Stmts)\n          =>\n-         Name(\"n\") ~> #capturePrimeLoopEntry\n+         Name(\"n\") ~> #capturePrimeLoopN\n          ...\n        </k>\n        [priority(1)]\n \n+  rule <k>\n+         N:Int ~> #capturePrimeLoopN ~> REST:K\n+         =>\n+         Name(\"divisor\") ~> #capturePrimeLoopD(N) ~> REST\n+       </k>\n+       [priority(40)]\n+\n   rule\n     <k>\n-      N:Int ~> #capturePrimeLoopEntry ~> _REST:K\n+      D:Int ~> #capturePrimeLoopD(N:Int) ~> _REST:K\n       =>\n-      #primeLoopEntry(N)\n+      #primeLoopEntry(N, D)\n*** Update File: /work/spec.k\n@@\n       #applyK(\n         toCall(primeLengthClosure),\n         (str(CS:IntSeq), .Vals))\n       =>\n-      #primeLoopEntry(isLen(CS))\n+      #primeLoopEntry(isLen(CS), 2)\n*** End Patch\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019f8dd7-bca4-7cd0-878f-9e3b9d3a324b"}}}
